/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-276729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/8c6e305056cc2128d2dffdbe4ae84cd21d7767dbfce67ca721a94cf24e54420d.png)\n\nGiven the sketch of a polynomial $p(x)$ above, find the solution to $p(x)>0.$\n\n$x\\in ($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)⋃(-2,$\n{{field-3}}\n$)⋃($\n{{field-4}}$,\\infty )$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-276729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the inequality $p(x)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=p(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is\n\n$$\nx\\in (\\,-\\infty ,-4)⋃(-2,0)⋃(1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/012cbba2f025420a8218565dc3a2877f5e5e9ac4da92f2f1afafe38be5c597ec.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-276729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40d53369556a3591f8a5fabb19914a539057ea8d02e671d5400829b03c8a88a4"} {"question" "q-276729" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" 