ows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/691c37edf48a5d7807f7c43d73b0ac014358632a1957e3016f953af6f47c8f36.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-4,1)⋃(3,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-270809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40d53369556a3591f8a5fabb19914a539057ea8d02e671d5400829b03c8a88a4"} {"question" "q-270809" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-270809" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-270809" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-270809" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/ho