an graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/24adb4d2477b6db5b51f538f5f3f57c197cbe3d1df53ad1b4e7e9479879f18dd.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $f(x)\\ge 0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is \n\n$$\nx\\in {-3}⋃[0,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-278843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40d53369556a3591f8a5fabb19914a539057ea8d02e671d5400829b03c8a88a4"} {"question" "q-278843" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-278843" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-278843" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-278843" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-87387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $P(x)={x}^{4}-{x}^{2},$ solve $P(x)\\ge 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-87387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the inequality $P(x)\\ge 0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & ={x}^{4}-{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x+1)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{4}-{x}^{2}$ are $x=-1,$ $x=0$ and $x=1,$  where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-1$ and $x=1$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/e6aa75d55f2776e3e2b5d029ad51ad9e39a80e49b613705a97fa01ff34113db5.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)\\ge 0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup {0}\\cup [1,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd5c48a023c450892602f94d85885db356a4d6569bc664f76e8806fb5a098947"} {"question" "q-87387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/activity-met